# The server image builds from the REPO ROOT (docker-compose.yml sets
# `context: .`) because it bundles both the backend and the dashboard built
# from client/. Everything the build does not need is excluded here — not just
# to keep the context small, but so editing the extension or the docs does not
# invalidate the image's build cache.

# Dependencies and build output — reinstalled/rebuilt inside the image
**/node_modules/
**/dist/
dist-extension/
extension.zip

# Produced by stage 1 of server/Dockerfile. A stale local copy must never be
# shipped instead of a freshly built one.
server/public/

# Uploaded resumes. Runtime data held in a Docker volume; a local copy must
# not be baked into the image.
**/uploads/

# Not part of the deployable
extension/
docs/
tasks/
assets/
deploy/
.github/
.husky/
.git/
.gitignore
.vscode/
.idea/
README.md

# Secrets and runtime artefacts. Env is supplied by docker-compose, not baked
# in; the cookie jar is a live LinkedIn session and the probe report holds the
# egress IP.
#
# EVERY pattern here needs the `**/` prefix. Docker matches these against the
# path relative to the context root and a bare `*` does NOT cross a `/`, so
# `.env` and `*cookies.json` match ONLY at the root. The context is the repo
# root, and the secrets live one level down in server/ — deploy.yml copies the
# live LinkedIn jar to server/linkedin-cookies.json immediately before the
# build. Without `**/` those files are baked into the image, and a later
# `RUN rm` would not help: the layer that added them keeps them.
.env
**/.env
.env.*
**/.env.*
*cookies.json
**/*cookies.json
probe-report.json
**/probe-report.json
.chrome-profile/

*.log
**/*.log
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store
